{"id": "8ed05276-3a1e-4a19-8506-1c6b3a6e0cd1", "timestamp": "2026-10-25T01:36:07.908217", "source": "user", "parent_id": "28a374b1-3110-4f86-a321-c490e44c2e0e", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Before we design the CoT-vs-no-CoT experiment for WorkArena++, please do a scoping pass only (no full solution yet):\\n\\n1) Inspection: check /workspace for any WorkArena++/ServiceNow ADK related material (task suites, config files, agent harnesses, existing baselines, prompt templates, seeds/splits, result logs). Report what actually exists vs. what is absent. Note the runtime constraints you observe (no network, no GPU, dependencies not preinstalled) and what that implies for a design-only deliverable.\\n\\n2) Proposed approach: sketch, at a high level, how you would structure a controlled comparison of chain-of-thought prompting against a matched non-CoT condition in WorkArena++. In the sketch, indicate (a) the unit of analysis and success metric you would adopt from WorkArena++ conventions, (b) the axes you would cross CoT with (e.g. model family/size, decoding temperature, task difficulty or app/domain strata, agent scaffolding such as ReAct-style vs. plan-then-act, tool-call budget), (c) how you would handle the known confounds specific to CoT (added output tokens/latency, extra prompt length, answer-format leakage, self-consistency-style sampling being smuggled in), and (d) what a clean primary contrast versus secondary contrasts would be.\\n\\n3) Assumptions and uncertainties: list the consequential assumptions you would be making, especially anything not established by the available sources. Flag explicitly where you are proposing a choice rather than reporting a source-supported fact (e.g. whether WorkArena++ tasks are long-horizon multi-step with tool calls, whether partial-credit progress metrics exist, whether trajectory-level success is binary, model/API access assumptions, and any compute/runtime budget).\\n\\nKeep this to inspection findings plus the approach outline and open questions. Do not produce the final experiment design yet.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"Will the chain-of-thought (CoT) prompting mechanism improve the task-solving ability of LLM-based agents in WorkArena++?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 224, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [\"neurips2024/97713/3:setup_1\"], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
