(binary success per episode, as adjudicated by the environment's built-in oracle/checks). Secondary: fraction of tasks solved with zero errors; number of environment steps; wall-clock; tokens/cost; failure taxonomy (spec-instruction following, tool-call errors, timeouts). If no partial-credit exists (I believe WorkArena++ uses binary success), we can add an exploratory \"goal-checklist coverage\" secondary metric constructed offline from the task's DB checks (counting satisfied sub-checks) — flag as my proposal, not a source fact.\n\n**Design structure**\n- Paired within-task design: each task instance run under CoT and matched no-CoT with everything else fixed (model, scaffolding, seed for task instantiation, tool set, budget).\n- Axes to cross (as a factorial with only some cells fully crossed; primary is a minimal pair):\n  1. Prompt condition: CoT (yes) vs. matched no-CoT (short direct answer/act-only) — primary factor.\n  2. Model family/size: e.g., a frontier closed-weight API model + a smaller open-weights model that can be self-hosted (2 sizes within one family if possible) to test whether CoT effects scale with capacity. Treat as stratification factor rather than full cross.\n  3. Decoding temperature: 0 (or greedy) vs. non-zero (e.g. 0.7/1.0) — because CoT's benefit may interact with sampling; also needed to justify repeated sampling.\n  4. Task difficulty/strata: task splits by category (single-app vs. multi-app/compositional), by number of required steps, by \"requires reasoning/common-knowledge\" tag; WorkArena++ has categories/domains (apps). Pre-register strata.\n  5. Scaffolding: ReAct-style interleaved think-act vs. plan-then-act (plan once then execute) vs. baseline framework agent (AutoGen/LangChain/OpenAI agent) — CoT is partly redundant with scaffold-provided reasoning; important confound control.\n  6. Tool-call / step budget and output-token budget: hold constant per arm and also report sensitivity.\n\n**Confound handling specific to CoT**\n- 