tes; concurrency limited by instance rate limits. Flag as assumption to confirm.\n\nClarification questions for the researcher (up to 6 questions in budget; propose ~5):\n1. Does the source (neurips2024/97713 setup_1) specify the exact task-suite size/splits, app categories, and per-task oracle (DB assertions) + whether any partial-credit/checklist metric exists?\n2. Which agent scaffolds and models does the source's baseline protocol use (AutoGen/LangChain/OpenAI/HF agents; GPT-4o), and is prompt modification permitted inside those frameworks or must the scaffold stay as published?\n3. Does the source expose per-step token/latency/cost logs and step limits — needed for cost-matched analysis?\n4. Are multiple independent runs per task supported (instance reset/seeding determinism), and is there a documented max step budget?\n5. Is any open-weights model option documented (for the model-size axis), or is the setup closed-API only?\n\nLet me do one final quick check on /usr/local/cuda and git availability, then hand off.\n\nActually cuda dir exists but no nvidia devices — check whether it's empty.\n", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"command": "ls -A /usr/local/cuda 2>&1 | head; echo \"cuda_ls_exit=$?\"; command -v git nvidia-smi pip3 python3; echo '--- hidden in workspace ---'; ls -la /workspace/.[!.]* 2>&1 | head; echo '--- python stdlib stats check (scipy-free) ---'; python3 -c \"\nfrom math import comb, sqrt, erf\np=sum(comb(20,k)*0.5**20 for k in range(15,21)); print('binom tail ok:',round(p,5)); print('erf ok:', erf(1.96/sqrt(2)))\n\"", "timeout_seconds": 60, "kind": "ExecuteCheckAction"}, "tool_name": "execute_check", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-bc0b7ac5b6efffed", "tool_call": {"id": "chatcmpl-tool-bc0b7ac5b6efffed", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "execute_check", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"ls -A /usr/local/cuda 2>&1 | head; echo \\\"cuda_ls_exit=$?\\\"; command -v git nvidia-smi pip3 python3; echo '--- hidden in wo