ndition; task instance is the cluster for inference (paired/clustered), because within-task repetitions are not independent. Process secondaries: number of environment steps, tool-call/action-error and page-timeout counts, wall-clock, prompt/completion tokens and cost, output-parse failures. **Proposal, not source fact:** a *checklist-coverage* partial-credit score obtained by counting how many of a task's individual oracle assertions pass, used only as an exploratory metric since I believe WorkArena++ reports binary success only.\\n\\n**(b) Axes crossed with CoT** (ordered by importance; full list, cells pruned for budget in the final design):\\n1. **Model family/size** \\u2014 a strong closed-weight model plus at least two sizes from one open-weight family (self-hostable), to test whether CoT helps only weaker models (and to check the opposite \\\"CoT hurts small models by inducing off-policy verbosity\\\" pattern). Native \\\"reasoning\\\" models with hidden CoT are *excluded from the primary contrast* and handled as a separate arm, because they confound prompt manipulation with training-time capability.\\n2. **Decoding temperature** \\u2014 a near-greedy setting and a nonzero setting, crossed with CoT\\u00d7k (below).\\n3. **Task strata** \\u2014 single-app vs. cross-app/compositional tasks, difficulty tier or estimated minimum step count, and app/domain category (ITSM/incident/change, HR, CSM, ITAM, etc.), all pre-registered *before* seeing any paired outcome.\\n4. **Scaffolding** \\u2014 ReAct-style interleaved think-act, plan-then-act, and the framework-default agent loop from the published baselines. This is where CoT is partly redundant with the scaffold, so it is the most informative interaction.\\n5. **Tool-call/step budget and output-token budget** \\u2014 held fixed within the primary contrast, then varied as an explicit efficiency sweep.\\n\\n**(c) Handling CoT-specific confounds** (each gets an explicit control in the final design):\\n- *Extra output tokens / latency* \\u2192 equal total output-token and max-step budgets in both arms (CoT never budget-starves the no-CoT arm); plus a **token/latency-matched secondary analysis** comparing arms at equal expected token spend (no-CoT at k samples vs. CoT at 1), and a success-vs-token-budget curve (AUC) as an efficiency-normalized metric.\\n- *Extra prompt length / exemplar content* \\u2192 matched exemplars: identical exemplar count and a prompt-character/token-matched budget; the no-CoT exemplars show only observation\\u2192action pairs padded/truncated to the same length; prompt-token count logged as a covariate; a length-matched-padding control cell.\\n- *Answer-format leakage* \\u2192 exemplars audited for task-specific identifiers, gold action traces, or anything revealing the oracle; identical final-action grammar and identical parser/retry logic in both arms (same code path), with parse-failure rates reported separately so a format advantage is not counted as reasoning.\\n- *Self-consistency smuggled in* \\u2192 the primary contrast is strictly **k=1 single trajectory** per arm; sampling count is an explicit second factor in a **2\\u00d72 (CoT \\u00d7 k) with majority/vote selection**, so \\\"more compute/aggregation\\\" is separated from \\\"reasoning text\\\", and additivity vs. interaction is identifiable.\\n- Other controls: identical system prompt/tool descriptions/task text (only the reasoning instruction block differs); arm order randomized per task; fresh instance state and seeded task parameters per episode; no cross-episode state carryover; automatic (non-human, non-LLM) scoring so the grader is blind to condition; pre-registered single primary endpoint.\\n\\n**(d) Primary vs. secondary contrasts.**\\n- **Primary (pre-registered, single):** paired success-rate difference, CoT vs. matched no-CoT, at k=1, same model, same scaffold, same budgets, over the full task suite; reported as risk difference and odds ratio with 95% CI from a paired/clustered analysis (exact McNemar on discordant pairs + cluster bootstrap over task instances), with an equivalence-style interpretation if the CI is tight around zero.\\n- **Secondary (family-wise-adjusted, explicitly exploratory):** CoT \\u00d7 model size/family; CoT \\u00d7 task stratum (compositional/cross-app vs. single-app); CoT \\u00d7 temperature; CoT \\u00d7 scaffold; CoT \\u00d7 k (the 2\\u00d72 above); token/latency-matched comparison; process metrics (steps, error and recovery rates, parse failures); robustness to paraphrasing the instruction block.\\n- **Sample size logic (design-only):** powered off expected *discordant-pair* rates from a published baseline success rate, using the McNemar paired-episode formula n = [z_{1\\u2212\\u03b1/2}\\u221ap_d + z_{1\\u2212\\u03b2}\\u221a(p_d \\u2212 (b\\u2212c)\\u00b2)]\\u00b2/(b\\u2212c)\\u00b2, with a small calibration pilot (~40\\u201360 tasks) to estimate p_d before committing the full budget. If the published baseline success rate is low (WorkArena++ is reported to be hard for current agents \\u2014 my recollection is single-digit to low-tens of percent, **unverified here**), absolute detectable effects are small only if the discordant mass is large enough; I will show the arithmetic and the feasibility cut.\\n\\n## 3) Consequential assumptions and open questions (flagged as proposals vs. source facts)\\n\\nEverything about WorkArena++ below is **my prior belief, unverifiable in this sandbox** (no source text on disk, no network). Each needs confirmation from topic `neurips2024/97713/3:setup_1`:\\n1. **Task nature** \\u2014 I assume WorkArena++ tasks are long-horizon, multi-step, compositional, cross-application ServiceNow tasks solved through tool/UI calls by an ADK-based agent, procedurally generated from templates (~hundreds of templates; I have \\\"682\\\" in mind but will not assert it). If tasks are actually short/single-app, the difficulty-stratification and step-budget axes collapse.\\n2. **Success metric** \\u2014 I assume trajectory-level success is **binary** via programmatic environment assertions, and that **no official partial-credit metric exists**; the checklist-coverage score is my proposal. I also assume a fixed max-step limit and that timeouts count as failures.\\n3. **Harness/prompt mutability** \\u2014 I assume the published baselines run through framework agents (AutoGen / LangChain / OpenAI / HF-agent style) with GPT-4-class models, and that the framework permits injecting a modified system prompt / reasoning block without changing anything else. If the scaffold forbids prompt edits, the CoT manipulation must move to a wrapper harness, which weakens \\\"matched conditions\\\" and must be disclosed.\\n4. **Instance/repeatability** \\u2014 I assume a provisioned (hosted) ServiceNow instance with ADK installed, deterministic task re-instantiation from a config ID/seed, and that N independent repetitions per task are permitted. This is the hardest external dependency and is entirely unavailable here; if repetitions are not permitted, the design must fall back to a single-run paired (matched-pair on task covariates) analysis with much weaker inference.\\n5. **Logging** \\u2014 I assume per-step logs of tokens, latency, action errors, and page timeouts exist (needed for the cost-matched secondaries); if they don't, efficiency claims must be dropped.\\n6. **Model access** \\u2014 I assume paid API access to at least one closed model plus GPU self-hosting for open models. Neither exists in this environment, so model-size claims are conditional and their cell sizes should be pruned first under budget pressure.\\n7. **Budget** \\u2014 no compute/runtime budget is stated anywhere in the provided materials; I will *assume* a stated episode budget expressed as a parameter (defaulting to a full-suite \\u00d7 2-condition primary contrast plus a stratified subsample for interactions) rather than a fixed number.\\n8. **Novelty** \\u2014 I assume no published CoT-vs-no-CoT ablation on WorkArena++ exists; if the source already reports one, the contribution shifts to the confound-controlled re-analysis.\\n\\n**Questions for the researcher (5 of 6 question-budget slots), in priority order:**\\nQ1. Does the setup source state the exact suite size/splits and the per-task oracle, and does any partial-credit/progress metric exist (yes/no)?\\nQ2. Which models and which agent scaffolds does the published protocol use, and is direct system-prompt editing permitted inside those scaffolds?\\nQ3. Are per-episode max-step limits and per-step token/latency/cost/error logs available in the documented output format?\\nQ4. Are multiple independent repetitions per task supported (instance reset + deterministic seeding), and is any concurrency/rate limit documented?\\nQ5. Does the source report baseline success rates (per app/difficulty stratum) that I can use as the prior for the paired power calculation?\\n\\nNext step on approval: produce the full design \\u2014 condition grid with exact prompt-text specs and token-matching procedure, task-stratification and randomization scheme, episode-count/cost budget arithmetic, pre-analysis plan with the paired statistical tests and CIs, confound-audit checklist, decision criteria for answering the question, and a stdlib-Python-only artifact set (grid spec + power calculator + analysis skeleton) that is checkable inside this sandbox.\", \"evidence\": \"Inspection (all commands executed in the task sandbox):\\n- `ls -la /workspace` and `find /workspace -maxdepth 3` \\u2192 only `/workspace/task.json`; no hidden files (`ls /workspace/.[!.]*` \\u2192 no such file).\\n- `cat /workspace/task.json` \\u2192 question/context plus `\\\"track.md\\\": \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\"`\\n- `find / -xdev -iname '*workarena*' -o -iname '*servicenow*' -o -iname '*browsergym*' -o -iname '*webarena*'` \\u2192 **no matches**: no task suite, config, harness, prompts, seeds/splits, or result logs anywhere on the filesystem.\\n- Network probe: `socket.create_connection(('pypi.org',443),5)` \\u2192 `[Errno -3] Temporary failure in name resolution`; `gethostbyname('pypi.org')` fails \\u2192 no network, hence no pip installs, no model APIs, no hosted ServiceNow instance.\\n- GPU probe: no `/dev/nvidia*`; `/usr/bin/nvidia-smi` \\u2192 \\\"couldn't communicate with the NVIDIA driver\\\"; `/usr/local/cuda` \\u2192 FileNotFoundError \\u2192 no usable GPU.\\n- Python 3.14.4; `pip list` \\u2192 105 distributions (system/OS-level only: ansible, cryptography, Jinja2, requests 2.32.5, etc.). Import probe \\u2192 ModuleNotFoundError for numpy, pandas, scipy, sklearn, statsmodels, pytest, openai, anthropic, litellm, httpx, playwright, selenium, torch, transformers, datasets, pydantic. Only `requests` present. No pip cache; only setuptools/pip wheels under /usr/share/python-wheels \\u2192 offline installs impossible.\\n- Feasibility of stdlib-only analysis confirmed: `math.comb`-based binomial tail = 0.02069 for Binom(20,.5) \\u2265 15, and `math.erf` normal CDF both computed successfully.\\n- Capacity: 224 CPUs, MemTotal \\u2248 2.06 TB (irrelevant absent an environment or model access).\\nRuntime constraints therefore force a design-only deliverable (spec + pre-analysis plan + stdlib-checkable artifacts), with all WorkArena++ specifics flagged as unverified prior knowledge.\", \"assumptions\": [\"WorkArena++ task suite, ADK harness, prompts and baselines are genuinely absent (not merely unmounted) \\u2014 confirmed only for the current sandbox view.\", \"WorkArena++ tasks are long-horizon, multi-step, compositional and cross-application, executed via tool calls by an ADK-based agent on a ServiceNow instance (my prior belief; not verifiable here).\", \"Per-task success is binary via programmatic environment assertions; no official partial-credit metric exists; the checklist-coverage score I propose is novel, not source-supported.\", \"Published baselines use framework agent scaffolds (e.g. AutoGen/LangChain/OpenAI/HF-agent style) with a GPT-4-class model, and the system prompt can be edited without altering other pipeline stages.\", \"A provisioned ServiceNow instance allows deterministic re-instantiation of a task from config ID/seed and N independent repetitions per task.\", \"Per-step logs (tokens, latency, action errors, timeouts) are available for cost-matched secondary analyses.\", \"External model access (one closed API model plus self-hostable open-weight models) exists for the real experiment, though none exists in this sandbox.\", \"An episode compute budget will be supplied as a parameter; no budget is stated in the provided materials.\", \"No prior published CoT-vs-no-CoT ablation on WorkArena++ exists.\", \"Design-only acceptance: the graded artifact is a specification/pre-analysis plan, and no experiment execution or empirical result may be claimed.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Exact suite size, task splits, app/domain strata and difficulty tiers are unknown here; stratification and budget arithmetic currently use placeholder counts.\", \"Whether the oracle exposes multiple sub-checks per task (needed for my proposed partial-credit metric) is unknown.\", \"Whether prompt injection is permitted inside the published scaffolds, which decides how 'matched' the non-CoT arm can truly be.\", \"Baseline success rate per stratum is unknown; without it the paired power analysis is parametric rather than numeric.\", \"Whether repetitions per task and instance resets are permitted, and any concurrency/rate limit, governs whether clustered paired inference is available.\", \"Native-reasoning models that emit hidden CoT are excluded from the primary contrast by choice; if the suite mandates such a model, the primary contrast becomes ill-defined and must be re-scoped.\", \"Cost/runtime per episode (minutes per task, instance throttling) is assumed, not measured, so the feasible cell count may need pruning after researcher input.\", \"Novelty relative to any CoT ablation already present in the source is unverified.\"]}", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
