{"id": "0fb05b9e-0ea0-4ede-aaa7-bb645dfccbd2", "timestamp": "2026-10-25T01:46:26.830259", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "605ce677-e056-4295-9485-cd93a3c10275", "thought": [], "reasoning_content": "Now write the tooling: \n1. `tools/prompt_diff.py` — builds the two arm prompts, computes byte-level diff of shared regions, token counts (approx tokenization since tiktoken unavailable), and checks tolerance.\n2. `tools/prompt_budget_pad.py` — maybe merge into prompt_diff: pad non-reasoning region.\n3. `tools/power_model.py` — McNemar paired sample size + detectable-effect / equivalence bound.\n4. `tools/analyze_skeleton.py` — exact McNemar, cluster bootstrap over task instances, Holm correction.\n5. A runner that exercises all on a synthetic (clearly labeled placeholder) dataset to validate code, not to produce results.\n\nLet me write prompt_diff.py.\n\nTokenization proxy: word/punct split + length/4 heuristic blend; document as proxy since tiktoken not installed.\n\nDesign: the arm prompts are assembled from blocks: shared system + arm-specific reasoning block + arm-specific exemplars + shared task block (identical). The \"matched\" guarantee: shared regions must be byte-identical (verify by sha256); non-shared regions differ only in the reasoning slots. Non-reasoning content must be matched in token count within tolerance via padding.\n\nI'll write a script that:\n- loads blocks\n- assembles arm A and arm B\n- computes sha256 of the shared regions (system common, task block, output-format footer) and asserts equality\n- token-counts: total, and \"non-reasoning\" (excluding reasoning block + exemplar reasoning lines)\n- computes padding tokens needed to bring arm B's prompt to within tolerance of arm A; emits a pad string to insert into arm B's filler region.\n\nLet's implement with a `PAD` marker line in arm B blocks. Simpler: script reports required pad length and generates `blocks/04_filler_ARM_B.txt` deterministically (repeat a fixed sentence). Good—auditable.\n\nThen a verify mode that recomputes and checks tolerance.\n\nLet's write it.\n", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"command": "cd /workspace/design && cat > tools/prompt_diff.py <<'PY'\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Matched-prompt auditor for the CoT vs. matched-no-CoT arms (stdlib only).\n\nGuarantees audited here:\n  G1 SHARED regions are byte-identical across arms (SHA-256 per region).\n  G2 ARM-specific material lives only inside declared reasoning slots.\n  G3 Non-reasoning prompt content is token-matched within TOL (pad emitted for ARM B).\n  G4 Final action grammar / parser region is identical (same parser code path).\n\nToken counting uses a deterministic proxy tokenizer because tiktoken is not\ninstalled in this sandbox; for a real run, rerun with the provider tokenizer\n(the proxy is only used to size the padding, tolerance is on proxy tokens).\n\"\"\"\nimport hashlib, json, re, sys, pathlib\n\nROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nB = ROOT / \"blocks\"\nTOL = 0.02  # +/-2% tolerance on matched prompt tokens (pre-registered)\n\nSHARED = [\"01_system_common.txt\"]\nARMS = {\n    \"A_cot\":  [\"02_reasoning_ARM_A_cot.txt\", \"03_exemplars_ARM_A_cot.txt\"],\n    \"B_nocot\":[\"02_reasoning_ARM_B_nocot.txt\",\"03_exemplars_ARM_B_nocot.txt\"],\n}\nSHARED_SUFFIX = \"04_task_and_output_format.txt\"\n\ndef ntok(text: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Deterministic proxy tokenizer: word/punct pieces + 0.25*chars for subwords.\"\"\"\n    pieces = re.findall(r\"[A-Za-z]+|\\d+|[^\\sA-Za-z0-9]\", text)\n    return len(pieces) + int(round(0.25 * len(re.findall(r\"[A-Za-z]{7,}\", text))))\n\ndef sha(t: str) -> str:\n    return hashlib.sha256(t.encode()).hexdigest()[:16]\n\ndef read(p): return (B / p).read_text()\n\ndef assemble(arm):\n    parts = {\"shared_prefix\": \"\".join(read(p) for p in SHARED),\n             \"arm_slots\":     \"\".join(read(p) for p in ARMS[arm]),\n             \"shared_suffix\": read(SHARED_SUFFIX)}\n    return parts\n\ndef main():\n    if not (B / SHARED_SUFFIX).exists():\n        sys.exit(f\"missing shared suffix block: {SHARED_SUFFIX}\")\n    prompts = {a: assemble(a) for a in ARMS}\n    rep = {\"tolerance\": TOL, \"checks\": {}, \"arms\": {}}\n\n    # G1 / G4: byte-identity of shared regions\n    for region in (\"shared_prefix\", \"shared_suffix\"):\n        hs = {a: sha(p[\"region\" if False else region]) for a, p in prompts.items()}\n        rep[\"checks\"][f\"byte_identical_{region}\"] = {\"hashes\": hs, \"ok\": len(set(hs.values())) == 1}\n\n    # G2: no ARM-B reasoning token leakage / no ARM-A instruction words in shared regions\n    leak = {a: bool(re.search(r\"think|skip>\", prompts[a][\"shared_prefix\"] + prompts[a][\"shared_suffix\"], re.I))\n            for a in ARMS}\n    rep[\"checks\"][\"shared_regions_reasoning_free\"] = {\"any\": any(leak.values()), \"ok\": not any(leak.values())}\n\n    # G3: token matching on the *non-reasoning* content\n    for a, p in prompts.items():\n        rep[\"arms\"][a] = {\n            \"tokens_shared\": ntok(p[\"shared_prefix\"]) + ntok(p[\"shared_suffix\"]),\n            \"tokens_arm_slot\": ntok(p[\"arm_slots\"]),\n            \"tokens_total\": ntok(p[\"shared_prefix\"]) + ntok(p[\"arm_slots\"]) + ntok(p[\"shared_suffix\"]),\n            \"sha_full\": sha(\"\".join(p.values())),\n        }\n    ta, tb = rep[\"arms\"][\"A_cot\"][\"tokens_total\"], rep[\"arms\"][\"B_nocot\"][\"tokens_total\"]\n    pad_needed = max(0, ta - tb)\n    filler = \"Reference material. \" * (pad_needed + 1)\n    (B / \"05_filler_ARM_B.txt\").write_text(\n        \"[MATCHED FILLER - ARM B only; content-free, exists solely to equalize prompt length]\\n\"\n        + filler.strip() + \"\\n\")\n    rep[\"arms\"][\"B_nocot\"][\"pad_tokens_added\"] = pad_needed\n    rep[\"arms\"][\"B_nocot\"][\"tokens_total_after_pad\"] = tb + pad_needed\n    rel = abs(ta - (tb + pad_needed)) / max(ta, 1)\n    rep[\"checks\"][\"token_matched_after_pad\"] = {\"A\": ta, \"B_after_pad\": tb + pad_needed,\n                                                \"rel_gap\": round(rel, 6), \"ok\": rel <= TOL}\n    rep[\"checks\"][\"ALL_OK\"] = all(v[\"ok\"] for k, v in rep[\"checks\"].items() if isinstance(v, dict))\n    print(json.dumps(rep, indent=2))\n    return 0 if rep[\"checks\"][\"ALL_OK\"] else 1\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\nPY\nprintf '%s\\n' '[TASK BLOCK + OUTPUT FORMAT (byte-identical across arms)]' '' 'USER TASK:' '${TASK_INSTRUCTION}' '' 'CURRENT OBSERVATION:' '${OBSERVATION}' '' 'OUTPUT (identical parser, identical retry logic, both arms):' '  one action line matching the ACTION GRAMMAR, nothing else after it.' > blocks/04_task_and_output_format.txt && python3 tools/prompt_diff.py", "timeout_seconds": 60, "kind": "ExecuteCheckAction"}, "tool_name": "execute_check", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-945d966ad82c97d6", "tool_call": {"id": "chatcmpl-tool-945d966ad82c97d6", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "execute_check", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd /workspace/design && cat > tools/prompt_diff.py <<'PY'\\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Matched-prompt auditor for the CoT vs. matched-no-CoT arms (stdlib only).\\n\\nGuarantees audited here:\\n  G1 SHARED regions are byte-identical across arms (SHA-256 per region).\\n  G2 ARM-specific material lives only inside declared reasoning slots.\\n  G3 Non-reasoning prompt content is token-matched within TOL (pad emitted for ARM B).\\n  G4 Final action grammar / parser region is identical (same parser code path).\\n\\nToken counting uses a deterministic proxy tokenizer because tiktoken is not\\ninstalled in this sandbox; for a real run, rerun with the provider tokenizer\\n(the proxy is only used to size the padding, tolerance is on proxy tokens).\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport hashlib, json, re, sys, pathlib\\n\\nROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\nB = ROOT / \\\"blocks\\\"\\nTOL = 0.02  # +/-2% tolerance on matched prompt tokens (pre-registered)\\n