{"id": "f10c8d66-a7f9-4420-9b69-b188075e94e7", "timestamp": "2026-10-25T01:46:42.858762", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "c5a5d848-d834-45e0-9b3d-dec8bb90fb30", "thought": [], "reasoning_content": "The auditor works. Now the leakage audit tool (scan exemplars for task-identifying tokens vs test tasks) — I can fold that into a second tool: `leak_audit.py` checking exemplar files for numeric IDs/table names/strings that appear in a provided task file (placeholder). Then power calculator, then analysis skeleton with McNemar exact + cluster bootstrap + Holm.\n\nLet me write power calculator: McNemar paired sample size given p10 (b: CoT-only success) and p01 (c: no-CoT-only success), alpha, power; plus detectable difference given n (equivalence-style: smallest RD the design can exclude / detect). Stdlib only: need normal quantile function (use statistics.NormalDist from Python 3.8+ — statistics.NormalDist is stdlib). Yes, `statistics.NormalDist().inv_cdf`. And binomial exact via math.comb / math.lgamma.\n\nThen analysis skeleton: reads JSONL of episodes, computes paired per-task success (majority over reps? no — pre-registered: per-task paired indicator using seeded representative run = first seed), exact McNemar (binomial on discordants), cluster bootstrap over tasks for RD, Holm correction over secondary family, stratified RDs, efficiency AUC placeholder.\n\nWrite both now.\n", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"command": "cd /workspace/design && cat > tools/leak_audit.py <<'PY'\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Answer-format / oracle-leakage audit (stdlib only).\n\nFlags any token in the ARM prompt blocks that could only have come from the\ntest tasks or the scoring oracle: instance identifiers, table/field names,\nrecord numbers, dates, URLs, and verbatim task-text n-gram overlap.\nUsage: leak_audit.py <exemplar_or_block_files...> [--tasks tasks.txt]\nExit code != 0 when any HIGH-severity finding is present.\n\"\"\"\nimport re, sys, pathlib, json, itertools\n\nHIGH = [\n    (r\"\\bSYS_[0-9A-Fa-f]{8,}\\b\",                 \"instance sys_id\"),\n    (r\"\\b(?:INC|CHG|RITM|SCTASK|HR|CASE|EA)[T]?\\d{5,}\\b\", \"ServiceNow record number\"),\n    (r\"\\b(?:sys_id|number|short_description|cmdb_ci|assigned_to)\\b\", \"raw field name (oracle-adjacent)\"),\n    (r\"\\b(?:assert|expected_|oracle|gold_action|ground_truth|check_that)\\b\", \"oracle/scoring vocabulary\"),\n    (r\"https?://\\S+\",                             \"URL / instance host\"),\n    (r\"\\b\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}\\b\",                    \"concrete date\"),\n]\nMED = [(r\"\\b\\d{4,}\\b\", \"multi-digit literal (possible parameter value)\")]\n\ndef ngrams(words, n=5):\n    return {tuple(words[i:i+n]) for i in range(max(0, len(words)-n+1))}\n\ndef main(argv):\n    files = [a for a in argv if not a.startswith(\"--\")]\n    tasks_file = None\n    if \"--tasks\" in argv:\n        tasks_file = argv[argv.index(\"--tasks\") + 1]\n        files.remove(tasks_file)\n    findings = []\n    for f in files:\n        txt = pathlib.Path(f).read_text()\n        for pat, label in HIGH:\n            for m in re.finditer(pat, txt, re.I):\n                findings.append({\"file\": f, \"sev\": \"HIGH\", \"kind\": label, \"hit\": m.group(0)[:60]})\n        for pat, label in MED:\n            for m in re.finditer(pat, txt):\n                findings.append({\"file\": f, \"sev\": \"MED\", \"kind\": label, \"hit\": m.group(0)[:60]})\n    if tasks_file:\n        tw = re.findall(r\"[A-Za-z0-9_]+\", pathlib.Path(tasks_file).read_text().lower())\n        tset = ngrams(tw)\n        for f in files:\n            ow = re.findall(r\"[A-Za-z0-9_]+\", pathlib.Path(f).read_text().lower())\n            shared = ngrams(ow) & tset\n            if shared:\n                findings.append({\"file\": f, \"sev\": \"HIGH\",\n                                 \"kind\": \"verbatim 5-gram overlap with held-out task text\",\n                                 \"hit\": \" | \".join(\" \".join(g) for g in list(shared)[:3])})\n    print(json.dumps({\"n_findings\": len(findings),\n                      \"n_high\": sum(x[\"sev\"] == \"HIGH\" for x in findings),\n                      \"findings\": findings}, indent=2))\n    return 1 if any(x[\"sev\"] == \"HIGH\" for x in findings) else 0\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))\nPY\nprintf 'Close INC0010042 and set the field assigned_to to the caller.\\n' > /tmp/placeholder_heldout_tasks.txt\necho \"--- audit on shipped exemplars (clean) ---\"\npython3 tools/leak_audit.py blocks/03_exemplars_ARM_A_cot.txt blocks/03_exemplars_ARM_B_nocot.txt blocks/02_reasoning_ARM_A_cot.txt | tail -8\necho \"--- audit on deliberately contaminated block (must fail) ---\"\nprintf 'EXEMPLAR 3\\nOBS: record INC0010042 open\\nACTION: action: fill_field(field=\"assigned_to\", value=Ab)\\n' > /tmp/bad_exemplar.txt\npython3 tools/leak_audit.py /tmp/bad_exemplar.txt --tasks /tmp/placeholder_heldout_tasks.txt | python3 -c \"import json,sys;d=json.load(sys.stdin);print('n_high=',d['n_high'],[f['kind'] for f in d['findings']])\"; echo \"exit_code_of_audit=$(python3 tools/leak_audit.py /tmp/bad_exemplar.txt --tasks /tmp/placeholder_heldout_tasks.txt >/dev/null; echo $?)\"", "timeout_seconds": 60, "kind": "ExecuteCheckAction"}, "tool_name": "execute_check", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-bf1bb5b910b6eee1", "tool_call": {"id": "chatcmpl-tool-bf1bb5b910b6eee1", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "execute_check", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd /workspace/design && cat > tools/leak_audit.py <<'PY'\\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Answer-format / oracle-leakage audit (stdlib only).\\n\\nFlags any token in the ARM prompt blocks that could only have come from the\\ntest tasks or the scoring oracle: instance identifiers, table/field names,\\nrecord numbers, dates, URLs, and verbatim task-text n-gram overlap.\\nUsage: leak_audit.py <exemplar_or_block_files...> [--tasks tasks.txt]\\nExit code != 0 when any HIGH-se