{"id": "ca81b3e6-c82e-4dec-9ef3-6924f2d89914", "timestamp": "2026-10-25T02:06:04.064926", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "ed8a5c42-7996-486d-bdf4-a263f6e9d3c7", "thought": [], "reasoning_content": "Everything is in place. Now hand off stage=result with the complete design in answer.\n\nI need to write the complete design in the answer field, coherent and complete, plus evidence with rationale, controls, feasible checks, repository observations.\n\nNote: don't print \"682\" as a suite size. I use 700 illustrative placeholder only, labeled.\n\nLet me write it comprehensively but not absurdly long. The DESIGN.md has the full text; my answer should present the complete design (the researcher sees the answer, not the files necessarily). I'll include the full design in the answer.\n", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"stage": "result", "answer": "# CoT vs. matched no-CoT for LLM agents in WorkArena++ — completed experiment design\n\n**Design only. No experiment was run; no outcome is reported or implied.** Every WorkArena++-specific quantity is a named parameter with a default and a sensitivity band, because the only source-backed statement available is the study objective (evaluate the effectiveness of CoT prompting for task-solving performance in WorkArena++); it does not state suite size, oracle granularity, scaffold internals, baseline success, step limits, logging fields, or reset/repetition policy. The suite size appears nowhere as a fact — only as a labelled placeholder (`N_TASKS`, illustrative 700) inside budget arithmetic.\n\nArtifact package (all stdlib-only, all executed successfully): `/workspace/design/` — `DESIGN.md`, `grid.json`, `MANIFEST.json`, `blocks/*` (the two arms' real prompt text), `tools/{prompt_diff,leak_audit,power_mcnemar,budget_model,analyze_skeleton,check_all}.py`. One command reproduces every offline guarantee: `python3 tools/check_all.py` → **14 PASS / 0 FAIL**.\n\n## 1. Estimand, hypotheses, metric\nPaired risk difference on the suite's task population: `RD = E_i[S_i(CoT) − S_i(no-CoT-matched)]` at k=1, one model, one scaffold. H1: RD>0; H0: RD=0; equivalence band ±RHO, RHO=0.03 (band 0.02–0.05). Secondary estimands: RD per stratum; the CoT×k interaction; RD at equal expected output-token budget; RD per scaffold.\n**Metric from WorkArena++ conventions:** per-episode binary task success from the suite's own programmatic post-hoc checks over instance/DB state (no LLM judge), aggregated to success rate, **task instance as the cluster**. Process metrics (steps, action errors, timeouts, tokens, wall-clock, parse failures) are secondaries. *Proposal, not a source fact:* checklist-coverage = fraction of a task's individual oracle assertions satisfied, used only if the oracle exposes sub-checks.\n\n## 2. Named parameters (unresolvable here, encoded as parameters)\n`N_TASKS` unset/band 50–5000 · `R_REPETITIONS` 3/1–5 · `MAX_STEPS` unset/10–60 (equal across arms) · `OUT_TOKEN_CAP` 1024/512–2048 (equal) · `WALLCLOCK_S` 180/60–600 · `PI_BASELINE` unset/0.02–0.60 · `PD_DISCORDANT` pilot-estimated/0.05–0.30 · `RHO_EQUIV_PP` 0.03/0.02–0.05 · scaffolds (3 assumed) · per-step log fields (assumed). Same table machine-readable in `grid.json → parameters`.\n\n## 3. Auditable \"matched\" arms (your item 1)\nArms differ **only** inside a declared reasoning slot; shipped text: `01_system_common.txt` (shared preamble/action grammar/stopping rules) · `02_reasoning_ARM_A_cot.txt` (`<think>…</think>` required before every action) · `02_reasoning_ARM_B_nocot.txt` (same-position `<skip>…</skip>`: identical turn structure, identical \"no action inside the block\" and finish rules, **no reasoning content**) · `03_exemplars_ARM_{A,B}.txt` (same K=2 exemplars, same observations, same actions; A additionally shows reasoning traces) · `04_task_and_output_format.txt` (shared task/observation/output-format region; the single shared parser and retry path live here) · `05_filler_ARM_B.txt` (content-free length filler).\n`tools/prompt_diff.py` attests: (i) SHA-256 byte-identity of shared regions — prefix `deda76396dc89edc`, suffix `f92d4b209c92e6b0`, identical in both arms; (ii) arm material confined to slots, shared regions reasoning-free; (iii) **token matching at ±2 %** — ARM A 649 proxy tokens vs ARM B 483 → 166 filler tokens added → 649, relative gap 0.0. Slot content is matched on *structure*, not on equal token count inside the slot, since a no-CoT arm cannot emit an equal number of reasoning-free tokens without smuggling content; length is therefore matched on the rest of the prompt and the filler length is reported. Tokenizer caveat: a deterministic proxy tokenizer is used because no provider tokenizer is installable offline; before any real run the script is re-run with the model's real tokenizer and filler regenerated.\n\n## 4. Confound controls (your item 2), each with a control *and* a residual-detection analysis\n| Confound | Control | Detection analysis |\n|---|---|---|\n| Extra output tokens / latency | equal `OUT_TOKEN_CAP` and `MAX_STEPS`; **co-primary** gives the no-CoT arm k>1 samples at equal expected output-token budget | success-per-1k-tokens, success-vs-token-budget AUC, token cost ratio |\n| Prompt length / exemplar content | filler-balanced at ±2 %; identical exemplar count, observations, actions | prompt tokens as covariate; C8 length placebo |\n| Answer-format leakage | one shared parser + one retry path; `tools/leak_audit.py` gate; no gold traces | per-arm parse-failure rate; failure taxonomy |\n| Self-consistency smuggled in | primary strictly k=1; `k` is a separate factor in a 2×2 | CoT×k interaction: additive ⇒ CoT ≈ extra compute |\n| Model confound | native-reasoning models excluded from primary (C7 descriptive, never pooled) | — |\n| Order / state carryover | per-task randomized arm order; fresh seeded instance state per episode | order-effect check, stratified RDs |\n| Grader bias | automatic oracle scoring, condition-blind by construction | — |\n\nThe leakage gate is itself validated by a planted contaminated exemplar (returns 2 HIGH findings, exit 1) while passing the shipped blocks (0 findings, exit 0) — it caught real `short_description`/`assigned_to` leaks in my first exemplar draft, which I then replaced with placeholders.\n\n## 5. Co-primary and primary contrasts\n**Primary (single pre-registered endpoint):** C1 = both arms × M1 × T=0.0 × framework-default scaffold × k=1 × all tasks. **Co-primary (first-listed, named, per your item 2):** C2 = token/latency-matched comparison at equal expected output-token budget plus the CoT×k 2×2 (k=1,5 majority). Rationale: for a multi-step agentic benchmark the likeliest reviewer objection is \"CoT just spends more compute\", so an effect that survives raw pairing but vanishes per token must be reported as more compute, not better reasoning. Secondary family: model size (C3), temperature (C4), scaffolding ReAct-vs-plan-then-act-vs-framework-default (C5), difficulty/app strata, paraphrase robustness (C9), length placebo (C8), native-reasoning model (C7).\n\n## 6. Grid, tiers, scope realism (your item 4)\nFull cross = 72 arm×model×temp×scaffold×k combinations per task per repetition → with the illustrative `N_TASKS=700`: ≈50 400 episodes at R=1, ≈151 200 at R=3 (≈25 200 holding k=1) — unrunnable, hence the tiered/blocked grid: **Tier 1 (never dropped) C1, C2; Tier 2 (stratified subsamples) C3–C5; Tier 3 (pruned first) C6–C9; Tier 0 pilot P0** (≈60 tasks × 2 arms × 3 reps) estimating `PI_BASELINE`/`PD_DISCORDANT`, excluded from confirmatory analysis. **Drop order: C9 → C8 → C7 → C6 → C5 → C4 → C3**; only then does scope shrink (C2's k 5→3, then R 3→2→1, then subsample fractions); C1 is never dropped or reduced — if C1 can't run, don't start. `tools/budget_model.py`: full tiered plan ≈ **38 202 episodes ≈ 79.6 serial days** (≈11.4 workers for a 7-day wall clock, before ServiceNow throttling, usually the binding constraint); the co-primary's k is the dominant cost (21 000 of 38 202) — `--cok 3 --cofrac 0.5` gives ≈23 500 episodes ≈49 days; tier-1-only floor ≈8 760 episodes ≈18 days.\n\n## 7. Procedure and pre-analysis plan (your item 3)\nPer episode: reset from config ID+seed and hash initial state → draw arm order from a seeded permutation → assemble prompt, refuse to run if region hashes mismatch → run under the cell's step/token/wall-clock caps logging raw completion, parse status, action, tool result, tokens, latency, error class → score with the suite oracle only → append one episode row → run both arms before inspecting anything.\nAnalysis (`tools/analyze_skeleton.py`): exactly one primary endpoint (RD, first-seed representative run per task-arm, no best-of-seeds); **exact conditional McNemar** on discordants; **cluster bootstrap over task instances** (B=4000, fixed seed) for the RD CI; per-arm Wilson intervals; **Holm step-down** across the secondary family. Feasibility modeling (labelled a model, not a result): `n = (z_{1−α/2}√pd + z_{1−β}√(pd − d²))² / d²`; illustratively at pi=0.10 (pd≈0.081) n≈252 pairs for d=0.05, ≈705 for d=0.03, ≈1588 for d=0.02; at a fixed 700 paired tasks d_detectable≈0.030 and the smallest effect **excluded** at 95 % is ≈0.021. **Decision rule:** \"improves\" iff McNemar p<0.05 AND bootstrap CI > 0 AND the co-primary does not attribute the gain to compute; \"no improvement (equivalence)\" iff the CI lies wholly inside ±RHO, reported as \"at this model/scaffold/difficulty mix CoT does not measurably improve WorkArena++ task solving and effects larger than RHO are excluded\" — never \"CoT cannot help\"; otherwise \"inconclusive\" with the achieved excludable effect size stated; a raw win that reverses in the CoT×k 2×2 is reported as \"aggregation, not reasoning\".\n\n## 8. Feasibility and fallbacks (your item 6)\nA real run needs a provisioned ServiceNow instance with the Agent Development Kit plus the suite, and model access — **neither exists here** (no network: DNS resolution fails; no GPU: no `/dev/nvidia*`, `nvidia-smi` cannot reach a driver; no numpy/pandas/scipy/playwright/openai). Fallbacks: no resets/repetitions → single-run matched-pair analysis (McNemar still valid on one paired run per task; equivalence claims dropped); no per-step token/latency logging → drop the co-primary and all efficiency claims, downgrade to outcome-only; one-bit oracle → drop checklist-coverage; harness forbids prompt edits → wrapper harness plus explicit disclosure of the weakened matched-conditions guarantee.\n\n## 9. Novelty hedge (your item 5)\nIf the source already contains a CoT ablation, the contribution becomes: a structurally matched non-CoT control (same turn structure, token-balanced prompt, shared parser) instead of a bare baseline; explicit separation of CoT from self-consistency via the 2×2; compute attribution via the co-primary; pre-registered paired inference with equivalence bounds instead of unpaired success-rate comparisons; and the scaffold-interaction result showing when CoT is redundant. Reproduction under those conditions is a valid outcome even if the direction is already known.", "evidence": "**Repository observations (what exists / what is absent).** `/workspace` contained only `task.json`; recursive listing plus filesystem-wide `find / -xdev` for `*workarena*`, `*servicenow*`, `*browsergym*`, `*webarena*` → **zero hits**: no task suite, templates, seeds/splits, ADK harness, agent scaffolds, prompt templates, config files, baselines, or result logs, and no source text for `neurips2024/97713/3:setup_1`. Hence every WorkArena++ specific is prior knowledge, encoded as parameters.\n\n**Runtime constraints measured.** Network blocked (`socket.create_connection(('pypi.org',443))` → `gaierror -3`; `gethostbyname` fails) → no pip installs, no model APIs, no reachable ServiceNow instance. GPU absent: no `/dev/nvidia*`, `/usr/bin/nvidia-smi` → \"couldn't communicate with the NVIDIA driver\", `/usr/local/cuda` does not exist. Python 3.14.4 with 105 system distributions; import probe → ModuleNotFoundError for numpy, pandas, scipy, sklearn, statsmodels, pytest, openai, anthropic, litellm, httpx, playwright, selenium, torch, transformers, datasets, pydantic (only `requests`). No pip cache or offline wheels → these constraints make the deliverable necessarily design-only, and drove the choice of stdlib-only artifacts (verified `math.comb`/`math.erf`/`statistics.NormalDist` suffice).\n\n**Feasible checks actually executed (all offline; no experiment, no WorkArena++ asset).** `python3 tools/check_all.py` → **14 PASS, 0 FAIL, exit 0**; `MANIFEST.json` holds SHA-256 of 15 shipped files. Specifically:\n1. Matched-prompt auditor: shared-region hashes identical across arms (prefix `deda76396dc89edc`, suffix `f92d4b209c92e6b0`); shared regions reasoning-free; token match A=649, B=483+166 filler → 649, rel gap 0.0 ≤ 0.02.\n2. Leakage gate: shipped blocks 0 HIGH findings/exit 0; **negative control** on a planted contaminated exemplar → 2 HIGH findings, exit 1. It caught genuine leaks in my first draft (`short_description`, `assigned_to`), which I then sanitized — i.e. the gate changed the artifact.\n3. Statistical validation against hand-computed references: exact McNemar matches binomial-tail values for (b,c) = (30,10)→0.002221, (1,0)→1.0, (5,5)→1.0, (60,40)→0.056888, (3,1)→0.625; Holm on {0.01,0.03,0.04} → {0.03,0.06,0.06}; Wilson(8/100) → [0.04109, 0.14998]. (Two of my initial \"expected\" values were wrong; the implementations matched the hand recomputations, which is why they ship.)\n4. Power engine calibration: at the null (b=c) it returns 0.037–0.045 ≤ α=0.05, and reproduces target power (0.774) for rd=0.05 at n=375.\n5. Two real bugs found and fixed by these checks: (a) the McNemar power routine initially built its rejection region under the alternative proportion instead of the null p=½, producing ~α \"power\" everywhere; (b) `power_exact` overflowed on large n (fixed with lgamma/log-space plus a labelled normal approximation above a cap), and the detectable-effect inversion was switched to closed-form inversion for tractability.\n6. Budget model runs: total 38 202 episodes, tier1+2 32 550, 79.59 serial days, 11.4 concurrency for 7 days at 180 s/episode; coprimary knobs → 21 000 / 10 500 / 6 300 episodes for (k=5,frac=1.0) / (k=5,0.5) / (k=3,0.5); tier-1-only floor 8 760 episodes ≈18 days.\n7. Spec-consistency check caught a contradiction in my own grid (C2 appeared both in `never_pruned` and in the pruning order); fixed by separating \"drop a cell entirely\" (tier-monotone [3,3,3,3,2,2,2], no tier-1) from \"shrink a cell's scope\", with C1 never reducible. Re-verified: all pass.\n8. Analysis-skeleton self-test uses **seeded synthetic** records only and validates code (RD sign, CI brackets the point estimate, Holm monotone) — it carries no information about WorkArena++ and is labelled as such in the artifact.\n\n**Novelty search limit.** With no network and no source text on disk I could not verify whether a CoT ablation already exists; §9 of the design is written to survive either answer.", "assumptions": ["WorkArena++ tasks are long-horizon, multi-step, tool-using ServiceNow tasks (prior belief; unverified here).", "Per-task success is binary via programmatic instance-state checks and is trajectory-level; no official partial-credit metric exists — checklist-coverage is my proposal, conditional on the oracle exposing sub-checks.", "Published baselines use framework agent scaffolds with a GPT-4-class model, and the system prompt can be edited without altering other pipeline stages.", "Instance state is resettable and deterministically re-seedable from a config ID/seed, and R repetitions per task are permitted (fallback design provided if not).", "Per-step logs of tokens, latency and error class exist, enabling the co-primary compute-attribution analysis (co-primary and all efficiency claims are dropped otherwise).", "For a real run there is paid access to one closed-weight model plus GPU self-hosting for two open-weight models; neither exists in this sandbox.", "No prior CoT-vs-no-CoT ablation exists in the source (unverifiable offline); §9 hedges this.", "No compute/runtime budget was supplied, so budget is a parameter of the budget model rather than a fixed number.", "Our design choices (not task requirements): RHO=0.03, R_REPETITIONS=3, temperatures {0.0,0.7}, k {1,5}, subsample fractions 0.35/0.12, exemplar K=2, token-matching tolerance ±2 %, proxy tokenizer pending the provider tokenizer.", "The suite size is unknown; 700 is used only as a labelled placeholder inside illustrative budget arithmetic."], "uncertainties": ["Suite size, task splits and app/difficulty strata are unknown, so all episode counts and power numbers are parameterized, not committed.", "Whether the oracle exposes sub-checks (partial credit) is unknown; if not, the exploratory progress metric disappears.", "Whether the real harness permits system-prompt injection — if not, the manipulation moves to a wrapper harness and the matched-conditions guarantee must be downgraded in the write-up.", "Baseline success rate and discordant-pair mass are unknown; the pilot P0 exists precisely to estimate them before the paired sample size is fixed.", "Whether repetitions/resets and per-step logging are available decides between the primary plan, the single-run matched-pair fallback, and dropping the co-primary.", "The proxy tokenizer may mis-rank long/short prompts relative to the provider tokenizer; the ±2 % match must be recomputed with the real tokenizer before running.", "ServiceNow instance throttling and concurrency limits are unmodelled beyond a serial-wall-clock estimate and could dominate the schedule.", "Native-reasoning models are excluded from the primary by choice; if the target deployment mandates such a model, the primary contrast must be re-scoped because hidden CoT is not manipulable by prompt."], "kind": "ReviewHandoffAction"}, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a29faccd86c23b34", "tool_call": {"id": "chatcmpl-tool-a29faccd86c23b34", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"stage\": \"result\", \"answer\": \"# CoT vs. matched no-CoT for LLM agents in WorkArena++ \\u2014 completed experiment design\\n\\n**Design only. No experiment was run; no outcome is reported or implied.** Every WorkArena++-specific quantity is a named parameter with a default and a sensitivity band, because the only source-backed statement available is the study objective (evaluate the effectiveness of CoT prompting for task-solving performance in WorkArena++); it does not state suite size, oracle granularity, scaffold internals, baseline success, step limits, logging fields, or reset/repetition policy. The suite size appears nowhere as a fact \\u2014 only as a labelled placeholder (`N_TASKS`, illustrative 700) inside budget arithmetic.\\n\\nArtifact package (all stdlib-only, all executed successfully): `/workspace/design/` \\u2014 `DESIGN.md`, `grid.json`, `MANIFEST.json`, `blocks/*` (the two arms' real prompt text), `tools/{prompt_diff,leak_audit,power_mcnemar,budget_model,analyze_skeleton,check_all}.py`. One command reproduces every offline guarantee: `python3 tools/check_all.py` \\u2192 **14 PASS / 0 FAIL**.\\n\\n## 1. Estimand, hypotheses, metric\\nPaired risk difference on the suite's task population: `RD = E_i[S_i(CoT) \\u2212 S_i(no-CoT-matched)]` at k=1, one model, one scaffold. H1: RD>0; H0: RD=0; equivalence band \\u00b1RHO, RHO=0.03 (band 0.02\\u20130.05). Secondary estimands: RD per stratum; the CoT\\u00d7k interaction; RD at equal expected output-token budget; RD per scaffold.\\n**Metric from WorkArena++ conventions:** per-episode binary task success from the suite's own programmatic post-hoc checks over instance/DB state (no LLM judge), aggregated to success rate, **task instance as the cluster**. Process metrics (steps, action errors, timeouts, tokens, wall-clock, parse failures) are secondaries. *Proposal, not a source fact:* checklist-coverage = fraction of a task's individual oracle assertions satisfied, used only if the oracle exposes sub-checks.\\n\\n## 2. Named parameters (unresolvable here, encoded as parameters)\\n`N_TASKS` unset/band 50\\u20135000 \\u00b7 `R_REPETITIONS` 3/1\\u20135 \\u00b7 `MAX_STEPS` unset/10\\u201360 (equal across arms) \\u00b7 `OUT_TOKEN_CAP` 1024/512\\u20132048 (equal) \\u00b7 `WALLCLOCK_S` 180/60\\u2013600 \\u00b7 `PI_BASELINE` unset/0.02\\u20130.60 \\u00b7 `PD_DISCORDANT` pilot-estimated/0.05\\u20130.30 \\u00b7 `RHO_EQUIV_PP` 0.03/0.02\\u20130.05 \\u00b7 scaffolds (3 assumed) \\u00b7 per-step log fields (assumed). Same table machine-readable in `grid.json \\u2192 parameters`.\\n\\n## 3. Auditable \\\"matched\\\" arms (your item 1)\\nArms differ **only** inside a declared reasoning slot; shipped text: `01_system_common.txt` (shared preamble/action grammar/stopping rules) \\u00b7 `02_reasoning_ARM_A_cot.txt` (`<think>\\u2026</think>` required before every action) \\u00b7 `02_reasoning_ARM_B_nocot.txt` (same-position `<skip>\\u2026</skip>`: identical turn structure, identical \\\"no action inside the block\\\" and finish rules, **no reasoning content**) \\u00b7 `03_exemplars_ARM_{A,B}.txt` (same K=2 exemplars, same observations, same actions; A additionally shows reasoning traces) \\u00b7 `04_task_and_output_format.txt` (shared task/observation/output-format region; the single shared parser and retry path live here) \\u00b7 `05_filler_ARM_B.txt` (content-free length filler).\\n`tools/prompt_diff.py` attests: (i) SHA-256 byte-identity of shared regions \\u2014 prefix `deda76396dc89edc`, suffix `f92d4b209c92e6b0`, identical in both arms; (ii) arm material confined to slots, shared regions reasoning-free; (iii) **token matching at \\u00b12 %** \\u2014 ARM A 649 proxy tokens vs ARM B 483 \\u2192 166 filler tokens added \\u2192 649, relative gap 0.0. Slot content is matched on *structure*, not on equal token count inside the slot, since a no-CoT arm cannot emit an equal number of reasoning-free tokens without smuggling content; length is therefore matched on the rest of the prompt and the filler length is reported. Tokenizer caveat: a deterministic proxy tokenizer is used because no provider tokenizer is installable offline; before any real run the script is re-run with the model's real tokenizer and filler regenerated.\\n\\n## 4. Confound controls (your item 2), each with a control *and* a residual-detection analysis\\n| Confound | Control | Detection analysis |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Extra output tokens / latency | equal `OUT_TOKEN_CAP` and `MAX_STEPS`; **co-primary** gives the no-CoT arm k>1 samples at equal expected output-token budget | success-per-1k-tokens, success-vs-token-budget AUC, token cost ratio |\\n| Prompt length / exemplar content | filler-balanced at \\u00b12 %; identical exemplar count, observations, actions | prompt tokens as covariate; C8 length placebo |\\n| Answer-format leakage | one shared parser + one retry path; `tools/leak_audit.py` gate; no gold traces | per-arm parse-failure rate; failure taxonomy |\\n| Self-consistency smuggled in | primary strictly k=1; `k` is a separate factor in a 2\\u00d72 | CoT\\u00d7k interaction: additive \\u21d2 CoT \\u2248 extra compute |\\n| Model confound | native-reasoning models excluded from primary (C7 descriptive, never pooled) | \\u2014 |\\n| Order / state carryover | per-task randomized arm order; fresh seeded instance state per episode | order-effect check, stratified RDs |\\n| Grader bias | automatic oracle scoring, condition-blind by construction | \\u2014 |\\n\\nThe leakage gate is itself validated by a planted contaminated exemplar (returns 2 HIGH findings, exit 1) while passing the shipped blocks (0 findings, exit 0) \\u2014 it caught real `short_description`/`assigned_to` leaks in my first exemplar draft, which I then replaced with placeholders.\\n\\n## 5. Co-primary and primary contrasts\\n**Primary (single pre-registered endpoint):** C1 = both arms \\u00d7 M1 \\u00d7 T=0.0 \\u00d7 framework-default scaffold \\u00d7 k=1 \\u00d7 all tasks. **Co-primary (first-listed, named, per your item 2):** C2 = token/latency-matched comparison at equal expected output-token budget plus the CoT\\u00d7k 2\\u00d72 (k=1,5 majority). Rationale: for a multi-step agentic benchmark the likeliest reviewer objection is \\\"CoT just spends more compute\\\", so an effect that survives raw pairing but vanishes per token must be reported as more compute, not better reasoning. Secondary family: model size (C3), temperature (C4), scaffolding ReAct-vs-plan-then-act-vs-framework-default (C5), difficulty/app strata, paraphrase robustness (C9), length placebo (C8), native-reasoning model (C7).\\n\\n## 6. Grid, tiers, scope realism (your item 4)\\nFull cross = 72 arm\\u00d7model\\u00d7temp\\u00d7scaffold\\u00d7k combinations per task per repetition \\u2192 with the illustrative `N_TASKS=700`: \\u224850 400 episodes at R=1, \\u2248151 200 at R=3 (\\u224825 200 holding k=1) \\u2014 unrunnable, hence the tiered/blocked grid: **Tier 1 (never dropped) C1, C2; Tier 2 (stratified subsamples) C3\\u2013C5; Tier 3 (pruned first) C6\\u2013C9; Tier 0 pilot P0** (\\u224860 tasks \\u00d7 2 arms \\u00d7 3 reps) estimating `PI_BASELINE`/`PD_DISCORDANT`, excluded from confirmatory analysis. **Drop order: C9 \\u2192 C8 \\u2192 C7 \\u2192 C6 \\u2192 C5 \\u2192 C4 \\u2192 C3**; only then does scope shrink (C2's k 5\\u21923, then R 3\\u21922\\u21921, then subsample fractions); C1 is never dropped or reduced \\u2014 if C1 can't run, don't start. `tools/budget_model.py`: full tiered plan \\u2248 **38 202 episodes \\u2248 79.6 serial days** (\\u224811.4 workers for a 7-day wall clock, before ServiceNow throttling, usually the binding constraint); the co-primary's k is the dominant cost (21 000 of 38 202) \\u2014 `--cok 3 --cofrac 0.5` gives \\u224823 500 episodes \\u224849 days; tier-1-only floor \\u22488 760 episodes \\u224818 days.\\n\\n## 7. Procedure and pre-analysis plan (your item 3)\\nPer episode: reset from config ID+seed and hash initial state \\u2192 draw arm order from a seeded permutation \\u2192 assemble prompt, refuse to run if region hashes mismatch \\u2192 run under the cell's step/token/wall-clock caps logging raw completion, parse status, action, tool result, tokens, latency, error class \\u2192 score with the suite oracle only \\u2192 append one episode row \\u2192 run both arms before inspecting anything.\\nAnalysis (`tools/analyze_skeleton.py`): exactly one primary endpoint (RD, first-seed representative run per task-arm, no best-of-seeds); **exact conditional McNemar** on discordants; **cluster bootstrap over task instances** (B=4000, fixed seed) for the RD CI; per-arm Wilson intervals; **Holm step-down** across the secondary family. Feasibility modeling (labelled a model, not a result): `n = (z_{1\\u2212\\u03b1/2}\\u221apd + z_{1\\u2212\\u03b2}\\u221a(pd \\u2212 d\\u00b2))\\u00b2 / d\\u00b2`; illustratively at pi=0.10 (pd\\u22480.081) n\\u2248252 pairs for d=0.05, \\u2248705 for d=0.03, \\u22481588 for d=0.02; at a fixed 700 paired tasks d_detectable\\u22480.030 and the smallest effect **excluded** at 95 % is \\u22480.021. **Decision rule:** \\\"improves\\\" iff McNemar p<0.05 AND bootstrap CI > 0 AND the co-primary does not attribute the gain to compute; \\\"no improvement (equivalence)\\\" iff the CI lies wholly inside \\u00b1RHO, reported as \\\"at this model/scaffold/difficulty mix CoT does not measurably improve WorkArena++ task solving and effects larger than RHO are excluded\\\" \\u2014 never \\\"CoT cannot help\\\"; otherwise \\\"inconclusive\\\" with the achieved excludable effect size stated; a raw win that reverses in the CoT\\u00d7k 2\\u00d72 is reported as \\\"aggregation, not reasoning\\\".\\n\\n## 8. Feasibility and fallbacks (your item 6)\\nA real run needs a provisioned ServiceNow instance with the Agent Development Kit plus the suite, and model access \\u2014 **neither exists here** (no network: DNS resolution fails; no GPU: no `/dev/nvidia*`, `nvidia-smi` cannot reach a driver; no numpy/pandas/scipy/playwright/openai). Fallbacks: no resets/repetitions \\u2192 single-run matched-pair analysis (McNemar still valid on one paired run per task; equivalence claims dropped); no per-step token/latency logging \\u2192 drop the co-primary and all efficiency claims, downgrade to outcome-only; one-bit oracle \\u2192 drop checklist-coverage; harness forbids prompt edits \\u2192 wrapper harness plus explicit disclosure of the weakened matched-conditions guarantee.\\n\\n## 9. Novelty hedge (your item 5)\\nIf the source already contains a CoT ablation, the contribution becomes: a structurally matched non-CoT control (same turn structure, token-balanced prompt, shared parser) instead of a bare baseline; explicit separation of CoT from self-consistency via the 2\\u00d72; compute attribution via the co-primary; pre-registered paired inference with equivalence bounds instead of unpaired success-rate comparisons; and the scaffold-interaction result showing when CoT is redundant. Reproduction under those conditions is a valid outcome even if the direction is already known.\", \"evidence\": \"**Repository observations (what exists / what is absent).** `/workspace` contained only `task.json`; recursive listing plus filesystem-wide `find / -xdev` for `*workarena*`, `*servicenow*`, `*browsergym*`, `*webarena*` \\u2192 **zero hits**: no task suite, templates, seeds/splits, ADK harness, agent scaffolds, prompt templates, config files, baselines, or result logs, and no source text for `neurips2024/97713/3:setup_1`. Hence every WorkArena++ specific is prior knowledge, encoded as parameters.\\n\\n**Runtime constraints measured.** Network blocked (`socket.create_connection(('pypi.org',443))` \\u2192 `gaierror -3`; `gethostbyname` fails) \\u2192 no pip installs, no model APIs, no reachable ServiceNow instance. GPU abse